{
  "_comment": "Declare the MCP servers this project uses. Delete the ones you don't need and add your own. The filename MUST be `.mcp.json` (dotfile) and the root key MUST be `mcpServers` — that is the project-scoped format AI tooling (e.g. Claude Code) looks for; anything else is silently ignored. NEVER hardcode API keys or tokens here: this file is committed to git. Use ${ENV_VAR} expansion and export the value in your shell, as in the _example_with_secret entry below (delete it). lore (the optional project memory) is deliberately NOT declared here: its key could only be written as ${VAR}, and project config overrides the user-level registration — in an app launched from the GUI the variable is empty, the header goes out as a bare `Bearer `, and lore answers 401. Register lore once per machine instead: `claude mcp add --scope user --transport http lore <server>/mcp --header \"Authorization: Bearer <key>\"`.",
  "mcpServers": {
    "notion": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.notion.com/mcp"
    },
    "firebase": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "firebase-tools@latest", "mcp", "--dir", "./firebase", "--only", "firestore,functions,auth,storage"]
    },
    "_example_with_secret": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "some-mcp-server", "--header", "Authorization:Bearer ${SOME_MCP_TOKEN}"],
      "env": {
        "SOME_MCP_TOKEN": "${SOME_MCP_TOKEN}"
      }
    }
  }
}
